      "id": "at-glance",
      "title": "At a glance",
      "body": "For travelers, Tôi mất hộ chiếu is the phrase to keep ready for \"I lost my passport\" in police, ambulance, hospitals, passports, and immediate safety. This is for when you need immediate help after losing your passport. Lost passport is a core travel emergency and should stay accessible. It works best when you focus on saying what went missing before you add where or when it happened. After you say it, listen for a question about the last place, a room or ride check, or a staff handoff; the next rows help you keep the exchange moving.",
